# Project Overview

This is a Nuxt 4 **Video Anatomizer** application - a "Mobbin for Video" tool that breaks down short-form videos into structured, reusable templates.

## Development Commands

```bash
pnpm dev          # Start development server
pnpm build        # Build for production
pnpm generate     # Generate static site
pnpm preview      # Preview production build
```

## Architecture

### Key Directories
- `app/pages/` - Route pages (dashboard, anatomize, view)
- `app/components/` - Reusable Vue components (video/, anatomy/, viewer/)
- `app/composables/` - Data fetching hooks (useVideos, useSegments, useLogicFlows, useSupabase)
- `app/types/` - TypeScript types and constants
- `supabase/schema.sql` - Database schema (run in Supabase SQL Editor)

### Main Pages
- `/` - Dashboard listing all videos
- `/anatomize` - Upload new video
- `/anatomize/[id]` - Edit video anatomy (segments, scripts, tags)
- `/view/[id]` - View template with copyable blueprints

### Data Model
- **videos** - Main content with metadata, scripts, and tags
- **segments** - Time-based sections (Hook, Bridge, Value, CTA)
- **logic_flows** - Skeleton types (PAS, Listicle, etc.)

## UI Framework

Uses `@nuxt/ui` v4 with Tailwind CSS 4. Key configuration:
- Primary color: indigo
- Icons: Phosphor icons (prefix: `i-ph-*`)
- Custom border radius: `--ui-radius: 0.125rem`
- Font: Geist
- Theme: Light only (configured in `nuxt.config.ts`)
- Docs at https://ui.nuxt.com/llms.txt

Icon usage example: `<UIcon name="i-ph-check" />`

### CSS Variables (Design Tokens)

Use Nuxt UI's CSS variable classes instead of hardcoded Tailwind colors:

**Background colors:**
- `bg-default` - Main background (white in light mode)
- `bg-muted` - Subtle background for containers
- `bg-elevated` - Elevated surfaces
- `bg-accented` - Accented backgrounds
- `bg-inverted` - Inverted background

**Text colors:**
- `text-default` - Default text
- `text-muted` - Secondary/muted text
- `text-dimmed` - Dimmed text
- `text-toned` - Toned text
- `text-highlighted` - Emphasized text
- `text-inverted` - Inverted text

**Semantic colors:**
- `text-primary`, `bg-primary` - Primary brand color
- `text-success`, `text-error`, `text-warning`, `text-info` - Status colors

**Border colors:**
- `border-default` - Default borders
- `border-muted` - Subtle borders
- `border-accented` - Accented borders

## Key Dependencies

- **@supabase/supabase-js** - Database and file storage
- **openai** - AI/LLM integration (for future auto-transcription)

## Supabase Setup

1. Create `.env` file with `SUPABASE_URL` and `SUPABASE_ANON_KEY`
2. Run `supabase/schema.sql` in Supabase SQL Editor
3. Create a storage bucket named `videos` with public access
